covalence (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: the pairing code must be confirmed on the PC; only an
    iPhone's profiles are accepted, never an input device.
  * Security: programs other than Covalence must be allowed by the user
    (notification) before calling, sending, pairing, forgetting the iPhone
    or installing an update; iPhone control is reserved to the app.
  * Security: updates installed by a root helper that copies the package
    and checks its SHA-256 again; LocalSend asks before every reception,
    20 GB cap, no plain HTTP peers; screen mirroring protected by a PIN.
  * Security: SMS codes filled in automatically only on the website they
    name (@site #code), HTTPS top frame only; notification text escaped;
    bMessage body read by its length; HID reports sent to bluetoothd only;
    rclone download checked against its PGP signature.
  * Messages: no duplicates from notifications replayed after a
    reconnection (iPhone date kept), replies to you in the right
    conversation, name-only conversations merged with the contact.
  * Messages: group messages stay in their group, a message sent from
    Covalence is no longer removed by an older identical one, copies
    matched per sender, one cache per iPhone (the old one archived),
    deleted conversations stay deleted, edited iMessages update in place.
  * Contacts: "Retry" asks the iPhone again; after a refusal Covalence
    asks every 30 s for 10 minutes.
  * App: lists are no longer emptied by a transient daemon error;
    reactions and late names show at once; Messages and Headphones icons.
  * Daemon: every D-Bus error is answered, sends go before contact reads,
    artwork and app icon caches are pruned.
  * Guide in the sidebar, above Settings; icons missing from the
    elementary theme replaced (Photos, Bluetooth, browser).

 -- Melvin Couwez <301110918+melvincouwez-alt@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0200

covalence (0.4.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pairing from the iPhone's Settings › Bluetooth: the PC is discoverable
    during the pairing window, nRF Connect is no longer needed.
  * Paired iPhone marked trusted, so its profiles are no longer refused.
  * The iPhone listed twice by BlueZ (bonded and LE objects) is one phone.
  * When the iPhone forgot the PC, retries stop (no more link flapping)
    and the Overview offers to pair again; "Forget" button.
  * Reconnection backs off from 10 s to 5 min and restarts after sleep.
  * No GATT subscription on BlueZ's cached services while disconnected.

